1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:01,660
Welcome.

2
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:09,472
This tutorial shows you how to access the
DEIHS Maintenance Management System source
code on GitHub.

3
00:00:09,652 --> 00:00:17,140
We will cover downloading the project, cloning
it with Git, getting write access, and pushing
your changes.

4
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:22,288
By the end, you will be able to work on the
project like a team member.

5
00:00:23,888 --> 00:00:33,128
The repository contains the complete JavaFX
application, the MySQL schema, the launchers,
and the documentation.

6
00:00:33,308 --> 00:00:37,916
Everything you need to build and run the
system is in one place.

7
00:00:38,096 --> 00:00:45,296
You can use the code to study the project, to
run it on your own computer, or to contribute
improvements.

8
00:00:46,896 --> 00:00:50,736
Before you start, decide what kind of access
you need.

9
00:00:50,916 --> 00:00:54,708
Everyone can read and download a public
repository.

10
00:00:54,888 --> 00:01:01,392
To push changes, you need a GitHub account and
an invitation from the repository owner.

11
00:01:01,572 --> 00:01:07,260
You also need a browser, and optionally Git,
which we will install in a moment.

12
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:18,460
Open your browser and go to github dot com
slash mccollybalagtas slash DevNexus dash
DEIHS dash MMS.

13
00:01:18,640 --> 00:01:23,608
The repository is public, so you can view it
without signing in.

14
00:01:23,788 --> 00:01:27,364
The main branch contains the latest working
version.

15
00:01:27,544 --> 00:01:33,520
Take a moment to read the README, because it
explains the setup and the demo accounts.

16
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:39,320
The simplest way to get the files is to
download a ZIP.

17
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:43,244
Click the green Code button, then choose
Download ZIP.

18
00:01:43,424 --> 00:01:47,480
Extract the archive into a folder you can find
easily.

19
00:01:47,660 --> 00:01:57,860
This gives you a snapshot of the code, but it
does not include Git history and it is not
connected to the repository, so you cannot push changes this way.

20
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:02,412
If you want to contribute, install Git.

21
00:02:02,592 --> 00:02:09,792
Download it from git dash s c m dot com and
run the installer, keeping the default
options.

22
00:02:09,972 --> 00:02:16,092
On macOS, Git is usually available after
installing the command line tools.

23
00:02:16,272 --> 00:02:19,800
On Linux, install it with your package
manager.

24
00:02:19,980 --> 00:02:25,668
Then open a terminal and run git dash dash
version to confirm it works.

25
00:02:27,268 --> 00:02:30,652
Before your first commit, tell Git who you
are.

26
00:02:30,832 --> 00:02:35,800
Set your name and the email address associated
with your GitHub account.

27
00:02:35,980 --> 00:02:39,268
These details appear in every commit you
create.

28
00:02:39,448 --> 00:02:45,688
Use the same email you use on GitHub so your
contributions are linked to your profile.

29
00:02:45,868 --> 00:02:49,084
You only need to do this once per computer.

30
00:02:50,684 --> 00:02:52,868
Now clone the repository.

31
00:02:53,048 --> 00:02:57,800
In a terminal, move to the folder where you
keep your projects.

32
00:02:57,980 --> 00:03:02,708
Run git clone followed by the HTTPS URL.

33
00:03:02,888 --> 00:03:10,640
Git creates a folder named DevNexus dash DEIHS
dash MMS and downloads the full history.

34
00:03:10,820 --> 00:03:13,748
Then move into that folder with cd.

35
00:03:15,348 --> 00:03:17,796
Here is what you will find inside.

36
00:03:17,976 --> 00:03:23,736
The src folder contains the Java source and
the FXML views.

37
00:03:23,916 --> 00:03:27,468
The database folder contains the SQL script.

38
00:03:27,648 --> 00:03:32,064
The docs folder contains screenshots and these
tutorials.

39
00:03:32,244 --> 00:03:37,428
The README explains setup, and the run scripts
start the application.

40
00:03:37,608 --> 00:03:41,712
The pom dot x m l file lists the dependencies.

41
00:03:43,312 --> 00:03:46,168
Read the README before running anything.

42
00:03:46,348 --> 00:03:53,716
It lists the prerequisites, the database
import steps, the connection settings, and the
demo accounts.

43
00:03:53,896 --> 00:03:58,144
The first tutorial video covers the database
in detail.

44
00:03:58,324 --> 00:04:02,668
Following the README in order avoids most
setup problems.

45
00:04:04,268 --> 00:04:10,076
Reading a public repository does not require
permission, but pushing does.

46
00:04:10,256 --> 00:04:13,424
Ask the owner to add you as a collaborator.

47
00:04:13,604 --> 00:04:23,156
The owner opens the repository settings, goes
to Collaborators, clicks Add people, and
enters your GitHub username with the Write role.

48
00:04:23,336 --> 00:04:28,952
You then accept the invitation from your email
or from the repository page.

49
00:04:30,552 --> 00:04:37,416
GitHub no longer accepts your account password
for Git operations over HTTPS.

50
00:04:37,596 --> 00:04:40,740
Create a personal access token instead.

51
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:47,496
Open your GitHub settings, go to Developer
settings, then Personal access tokens.

52
00:04:47,676 --> 00:04:54,732
Create a fine-grained token limited to this
repository with read and write access to
contents.

53
00:04:54,912 --> 00:04:58,488
Use the token as the password when Git asks.

54
00:05:00,088 --> 00:05:03,520
As an alternative, use an SSH key.

55
00:05:03,700 --> 00:05:11,356
Generate a key with ssh dash keygen, using the
ed25519 algorithm.

56
00:05:11,536 --> 00:05:18,400
Copy the public key and add it to GitHub under
Settings, SSH and GPG keys.

57
00:05:18,580 --> 00:05:23,884
Test the connection with ssh dash T git at
github dot com.

58
00:05:24,064 --> 00:05:30,400
Once it works, clone with the SSH URL instead
of HTTPS.

59
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:34,184
Here is the daily workflow.

60
00:05:34,364 --> 00:05:37,868
Start by pulling the latest changes with git
pull.

61
00:05:38,048 --> 00:05:41,912
Create a branch for your work with git switch
dash c.

62
00:05:42,092 --> 00:05:46,916
Make your edits, then review them with git
status and git diff.

63
00:05:47,096 --> 00:05:53,672
Stage the files with git add, commit with a
clear message, and push the branch to GitHub.

64
00:05:53,852 --> 00:05:57,428
Never work directly on main for team changes.

65
00:05:59,028 --> 00:06:02,508
After pushing a branch, open a pull request.

66
00:06:02,688 --> 00:06:06,096
GitHub shows a Compare and pull request
button.

67
00:06:06,276 --> 00:06:10,404
Describe what you changed and why, then
request a review.

68
00:06:10,584 --> 00:06:17,352
The owner or another member reviews the code,
discusses any issues, and merges it into main.

69
00:06:17,532 --> 00:06:23,076
Pull requests keep the main branch stable and
give everyone a chance to review.

70
00:06:24,676 --> 00:06:27,796
These are the errors you are most likely to
meet.

71
00:06:27,976 --> 00:06:35,656
Repository not found usually means the URL is
wrong or you are not signed in to a private
repository.

72
00:06:35,836 --> 00:06:40,252
Authentication failed means your token is
missing or expired.

73
00:06:40,432 --> 00:06:45,856
Permission denied publickey means your SSH key
is not registered.

74
00:06:46,036 --> 00:06:52,012
A rejected push means someone else pushed
first, so pull before you push again.

75
00:06:53,612 --> 00:06:56,852
A few rules keep the repository healthy.

76
00:06:57,032 --> 00:07:01,832
Never commit database passwords, tokens, or
personal data.

77
00:07:02,012 --> 00:07:05,972
Keep db dot properties free of real
credentials.

78
00:07:06,152 --> 00:07:12,872
Do not commit the target folder or IDE files;
the gitignore file already excludes them.

79
00:07:13,052 --> 00:07:19,196
Pull before you start, use clear commit
messages, and never force push to main.

80
00:07:20,796 --> 00:07:25,836
That is everything you need to access and
contribute to the repository.

81
00:07:26,016 --> 00:07:33,432
You can download the ZIP to explore, clone
with Git to develop, and open a pull request
to share your work.

82
00:07:33,612 --> 00:07:36,804
The links are in the description and in the
README.

83
00:07:36,984 --> 00:07:39,888
Thanks for watching, and happy building.
